rations in Canada, Mexico, Peru, Chile, Colombia and the Caribbean. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 8.4% to C$36.4B in fiscal 2025 (ended Oct 31, 2025). Net interest income rose 11.8% to C$21.5B and noninterest income rose 3.9% to C$14.8B; noninterest expense rose 8.0%, and the provision for credit losses was C$4.7B, versus C$4.1B.","Net income to common fell 0.3% to C$7.3B, or C$5.67 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 58.1% versus 58.3%. Scotiabank returned C$6.3B through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 8.4% to C$36.4B.","Net interest income rose 11.8%.","Noninterest income rose 3.9%.","Efficiency ratio improved to 58.1%."],"watch":["Net income to common fell 0.3% to C$7.3B.","Credit-loss provision rose 16.4% to C$4.7B.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was C$21.1B, up 8.0%."],"table":[["Total revenue",36.355,33.534,1],["Net interest income",21.522,19.252],["Noninterest income",14.833,14.282],["Noninterest expense",21.132,19.559],["Provision for credit losses",4.714,4.051],["Pre-tax income",10.509,9.924,1],["Income tax",2.751,2.032],["Noncontrolling interests",0.031,-0.134],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.528,0.472],["Net income to common",7.261,7.286,1],["Diluted EPS (C$)",5.673076,5.874188,0,"eps"],["Book value per share (C$)",70.262555,66.18984,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["The Bank of Nova Scotia Form 40-F filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000009631&type=40-F"],["Scotiabank financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/bns/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 59% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 59 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"C$36.4B","sub":"revenue · +8.4%","lines":["Net interest income C$21.5B","Noninterest income C$14.8B"],"cap":"Revenue rose 8.4% to C$36.4B.","say":"Revenue rose 8.4% to C$36.4B."},{"kicker